From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Ask for a mode by preference before weighing the list

A mode is chosen by how much of the shared picture it shows, and between two
that show it equally well, by which is larger. That answers for detail and
says nothing about motion. A receiver offering both 1920x1080 at 30 Hz and
1280x720 at 60 Hz is asked for the first because it is the larger picture,
and the second is never weighed at all, however little of what is being
shared is standing still.

Which of the two is wanted is not something the numbers decide. Half the
pixels at twice the rate is the same work either way, and on this link the
same bitrate comes to slightly more per pixel at the smaller size, so
neither is the careful choice and the larger one is not the safe default it
looks like.

Modes can now be named, in order, and are asked for ahead of the weighing. A
receiver that offers none of them is chosen for exactly as before, so naming
a preference costs nothing where it cannot be met, and the one named is said
in the log so a session shows which way it went.

One mode is named: 1280x720 at 60 Hz.

diff -ruN a/src/wfd/wfd-client.c b/src/wfd/wfd-client.c
--- a/src/wfd/wfd-client.c
+++ b/src/wfd/wfd-client.c
@@ -239,6 +239,28 @@
  * resynchronise for, which showed as the picture flashing. A receiver that
  * offers CEA modes is saying which timings it is made for.
  */
+/* Modes to ask a receiver for before weighing its whole list.
+ *
+ * What is weighed otherwise is how much of the shared picture a mode shows,
+ * and between two modes that show it equally well, the larger. That answers
+ * for detail and says nothing about motion: a receiver offering both
+ * 1920x1080 at 30 Hz and 1280x720 at 60 Hz is asked for the first, because
+ * it is the larger picture, and the second is never considered however
+ * little of it is standing still.
+ *
+ * A mode named here is taken when the receiver offers it, in the order
+ * written. A receiver offering none of them is chosen for as before, so a
+ * preference costs nothing where it cannot be met.
+ */
+static const struct
+{
+  gint width;
+  gint height;
+  gint refresh_rate;
+} wfd_preferred_modes[] = {
+  { 1280, 720, 60 },
+};
+
 static WfdResolution *
 wfd_client_best_mode (WfdVideoCodec *codec, gint width, gint height)
 {
@@ -246,6 +268,26 @@
   g_autoptr(GList) all = wfd_video_codec_get_resolutions (codec);
   WfdResolution *best = NULL;
 
+  for (gsize i = 0; i < G_N_ELEMENTS (wfd_preferred_modes); i++)
+    {
+      for (GList *item = all; item; item = item->next)
+        {
+          WfdResolution *candidate = (WfdResolution *) item->data;
+
+          if (candidate->interlaced)
+            continue;
+
+          if (candidate->width == wfd_preferred_modes[i].width &&
+              candidate->height == wfd_preferred_modes[i].height &&
+              candidate->refresh_rate == wfd_preferred_modes[i].refresh_rate)
+            {
+              g_message ("WfdClient: The receiver offers %ix%i@%i, which is asked for ahead of its own best.",
+                         candidate->width, candidate->height, candidate->refresh_rate);
+              return candidate;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
   preferred = wfd_video_codec_get_resolutions_cea (codec);
   best = wfd_client_pick_resolution (preferred, width, height);
 
